FastMinors -- faster linear algebra, especially for computation of minors
*************************************************************************

Description
===========

FastMinors is a package for computing relevant minors (determinants of
submatrices) of matrices of polynomial functions quickly

This package provides functionality for doing certain linear algebra operations
over rings quickly.  There is also some multithreaded capability which is
disabled by default.  Note this package was previously called FastLinAlg.

Tutorials:
There are tutorials on how to use various strategies and options in *note
FastMinorsStrategyTutorial: FastMinorsStrategyTutorial, and *note
RegularInCodimensionTutorial: RegularInCodimensionTutorial, which we recommend
the user explore if they are interested in the more advanced features of the
package.

Useful functions:
  * *note chooseGoodMinors: chooseGoodMinors, Tries to find interesting minors
    of a matrix.
  * *note isRankAtLeast: isRankAtLeast, Tries to show that a matrix has rank at
    least a given number by looking at submatrices
  * *note regularInCodimension: regularInCodimension, checks whether a ring is
    regular in codimension n, but doesn't return false.
  * *note projDim: projDim, checks the projective dimension of a module and may
    give better answers than *note pdim: (Macaulay2Doc)pdim, in the case that R
    is not homogeneous
  * *note recursiveMinors: recursiveMinors, provides a different strategy for
    computing minors of a matrix.  It is a cofactor strategy where the
    determinants of smaller minors are stored.
  * *note isCodimAtLeast: isCodimAtLeast, provides a way for finding lower
    bounds for the codimension of an ideal, without actually computing the
    codimension.
Many of these functions have extensive options for finetuning their behavior,
for instance by controlling how submatrices are chosen.  See the documentation
for *note StrategyDefault: StrategyDefault,

