chooseRandomSubmatrix -- returns coordinates for a random submatrix
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        chooseRandomSubmatrix(n1, M1)
  * Inputs:
      * n1, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * M1, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

This returns a list with two entries, first a list of random rows, and then a
list of random columns.  These specify a random submatrix of the desired size,
{\tt n1}.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M=matrix{{x^2,x^3,x^4},{y^4,y^2,y^3},{z^3,z^4,z^2}};|
|                                                         |
|             3      3                                    |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : chooseRandomSubmatrix(2, M)                         |
|                                                         |
|o3 = {{1, 2}, {1, 2}}                                    |
|                                                         |
|o3 : List                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

