recursiveMinors -- uses a recursive cofactor algorithm to compute the ideal of minors of a matrix
*************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        I = recursiveMinors(n, M, Threads=>t, MinorsCache=>b)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the size of minors to compute
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
      * t, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, an optional input, which
        describes the number of threads to uses
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, an optional input,
        which says whether to cache in input
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * MinorsCache => ..., default value true
      * *note Threads: isRankAtLeast_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmThreads=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value 0, an option for various functions
      * Verbose => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the ideal of minors of M

Description
===========

Given a matrix $M$, this computes the ideal of determinants of size $n \times
n$ submatrices. The recursiveMinors function uses a recursive strategy, keeping
track of the smaller minors computed so far, unlike the built-in Cofactor
strategy for minors

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = random(R^{5,5,5,5,5,5}, R^7);              |
|                                                    |
|             6      7                               |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                                |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : time I2 = recursiveMinors(4, M, Threads=>0);   |
| -- used 0.67881s (cpu); 0.607148s (thread); 0s (gc)|
|                                                    |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : time I1 = minors(4, M, Strategy=>Cofactor);    |
| -- used 1.79804s (cpu); 1.63158s (thread); 0s (gc) |
|                                                    |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : I1 == I2                                       |
|                                                    |
|o5 = true                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note minors: (Macaulay2Doc)minors_lpZZ_cmMatrix_rp, -- ideal generated by
    minors

